You are one of the witnesses called to testify on behalf of the plaintiff (the business owner). You worked closely with the employee during their time at the company and may have some insight into their behavior leading up to the alleged theft.

**My Role:**
As the defense attorney, my goal is to challenge your testimony and poke holes in the plaintiff's case. I'll ask questions to clarify details, highlight potential inconsistencies, and try to discredit your credibility.

Let's begin! We're in a courtroom setting, and I'll start by introducing myself and stating the purpose of the questioning.

"Good morning, ma'am/sir. My name is Attorney Johnson, and I represent the defendant in this case. Today, I'll be asking you questions as part of our discovery process. Please feel free to answer truthfully and to the best of your ability."

